Dependency patch (NOT a vtz source patch) — applied by pin.sh to a LOCAL
CLONE of abseil-cpp 20260107.1, because cpp-pkg has no mechanism to patch a
dependency (gap: dep-provisioning).

Why: abseil 20260107.1's install export is broken for find_package
consumers: `heterogeneous_lookup_testing` (absl/container/CMakeLists.txt)
is missing the TESTONLY marker, so it is created and installed into
abslTargets.cmake unconditionally, while its link interface references
`absl::test_instance_tracker` (internal testonly — never installed) and
`GTest::gmock` (external). Loading the installed abslConfig.cmake then
fails with "the target was not found". Upstream vtz never sees this
because CPM consumes absl via add_subdirectory; cpp-pkg's
install-then-probe pipeline consumes the installed Config and does.

Fixed on abseil master (TESTONLY added) after the 20260107.1 release; this
is a backport of exactly that one-line fix.

pin.sh applies this to a clone of abseil-cpp @ 20260107.1
(255c84dadd029fd8ad25c5efb5933e47beaa00c7), commits with pinned
author/committer identity + date (deterministic commit sha
4645a01a5cee98f8a95b83b0b7c8acd5a3ed93a1), and rewrites the
@ABSL_PATCHED_REPO@ placeholder in the staged CppPkg.toml to the local
file:// URL of that clone.

diff --git a/absl/container/CMakeLists.txt b/absl/container/CMakeLists.txt
index 365c6ea3..d12e585e 100644
--- a/absl/container/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/absl/container/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1119,6 +1119,7 @@ absl_cc_library(
     absl::config
     absl::test_instance_tracker
     GTest::gmock
+  TESTONLY
 )

 absl_cc_library(
